#### Describe the bug

After updating my container from 1.7.7.8 to 1.7.8, the modules i'm working on that uses some of the display hooks in order view, produces a render error. The two hooks i tried to use are: `displayAdminOrderMain` and `displayAdminOrderSide`.

Before upgrading everything worked fine, so i'm fairly sure this is a bug.

The error(i screenshot the whole profiler down below):
```
An exception has been thrown during the rendering of a template ("Expected argument of type "Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request", "NULL" given").
```
#### Steps to reproduce
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Hello @krekken & @maldarol
> 
> Could you please provide clear and concise steps to reproduce the issue pray Please check and feedback.
> 
> Thanks!

i made a module, that reproduces the problem, but i'll describe what i did, in case you don't want to rely on that. 
https://github.com/krekken/ordererrorreproduce

So i installed the hook like this, in the main php file:

```php

    public function install()
    {
        Configuration::updateValue('ORDERERRORREPRODUCE_LIVE_MODE', false);

        return parent::install() &&
            $this->registerHook('header') &&
            $this->registerHook('displayAdminOrderMain') && //this is the hook
            $this->registerHook('backOfficeHeader');
    }
```
And then i made a form inside the hook. 
```php
    public function hookDisplayAdminOrderMain(array $params)
    {
        $task = new Task();
        $task->setTask('Write a blog post');
        $task->setDueDate(new \DateTime('tomorrow'));

        $formFactory = $this->get('form.factory');
        $form = $formFactory->createBuilder()
            ->add('task', TextType::class)
            ->add('dueDate', DateType::class)
            ->add('save', SubmitType::class, ['label' => 'Create Task'])
            ->getForm();

        $form->handleRequest($params['request']);

        return $this->render('@Modules/ordererrorreproduce/views/templates/admin/error.html.twig', [
            'form' => $form->createView(),
        ]);
    }
```
Entity of the form:
```php
<?php 
namespace OrderError\Form\Entity;

class Task
{
    protected $task;
    protected $dueDate;

    public function getTask(): string
    {
        return $this->task;
    }

    public function setTask(string $task): void
    {
        $this->task = $task;
    }

    public function getDueDate(): ?\DateTime
    {
        return $this->dueDate;
    }

    public function setDueDate(?\DateTime $dueDate): void
    {
        $this->dueDate = $dueDate;
    }
}
```

the twig:
```twig
{% block content %}
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
        {{ form(form) }}
    </div>
</div>    
{% endblock %}
```

this module will work in 1.7.7.8, but will produce error in 1.7.8. the reason behind it, is that the request is missing from the $params array that the hook provides. Meaning, the issue is that the form here " $form->handleRequest($params['request']);", gets NULL, but in order to handle the form made with form.factory inside the hook, you need that request, but after the update from 1.7.7.8 to 1.7.8 that request object is missing.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


1. Call the `displayAdminOrderMain` hook in `ps_qualityassurance` module while this hook display its params:
```
public function hookDisplayAdminOrderMain(array $params)
    {
          dump($params);
    }
```

2. BO > SELL > Orders > Edit an Order
3. Check the results below, it display the params
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23308427/140385070-ae7c0331-894a-4a2b-b559-177a514f99bf.png)

4. Upgrade your shop to 1.7.8.0
5. BO > SELL > Orders > Edit an Order
6. See error > some params are not displayed
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23308427/140385189-3a4ec3ba-8fb1-47b8-95fd-a53edbd17595.png)

**Screenshots**
The error in symfony profiler
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23308427/140385283-f4c56be7-b573-4e97-a855-f5b913886de8.png)

#### Additional information

* PrestaShop version: 1.7.8.0
* PHP version: 7.4.24

#### Describe the bug

Prestashop class **Module** (`Prestashop /classes/module/Module.php`) has a function called **isCached** to check if tpl file is cached. This function fails to check and returns **false** while tpl is cached. 

Commit https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/pull/13804

Person who made PR was fixing issue #9763 and modified Module's class function **fetch** adding this:

```
if ($compile_id === null) {
            $compile_id = Context::getContext()->shop->theme->getName();
        }
```
Because of this change when you call **fetch** function with **$compile_id = null** it generates smarty cache file under $compile_id directory which is theme name in this case (if $compile_id is null then $compile_id is set to theme name).

But when you try to check if template is cached with function **isCached** with **$compile_id = null** you always get **false** because code added in **fetch** function should be also added to **isCached** function.

Templates are fetched (cached) under compile_id which is theme name in most cases, but isCached function checks if template is cached with empty compile_id which causes false result.

**This bug causes a huge performance issues.** Many plugins check if tpl is cached and if not - they perform data aggregation and assignation for smarty to render tpl but actually is not needed. 

#### Steps to Reproduce

1. Turn on debug profiling;
2. Open Prestashop Front Office and check executed SQL queries count;
3. Add this code 

```
if ($compile_id === null) {
            $compile_id = Context::getContext()->shop->theme->getName();
        }
```

4. in the beggining of **Module** (`Prestashop /classes/module/Module.php`) class function **isCached**;
5. Open Prestashop Front Office in separate window and check SQL queries count;
6. Second time queries count should be lower;

#### Additional information

* PrestaShop version: From 1.7.7.0
* PHP version: N/A

### Prerequisites

